          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في حال — fī ḥāl — \"in case\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في حال تأخر القطار، سأتصل بك. fī ḥāl taʾakhkhara al-qiṭār, sa-attaṣilu bik. In case the train is late, I will call you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also في حالة, fī ḥālat: in the event of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في حال (fī ḥāl) joins fī, \"in\", with ḥāl, \"a state, a condition\", built on the native Arabic root ḥ-w-l, \"to change, to turn\" (Lane). Literally, in the state that."
            }
          ]
        },
